{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777678752,"nonce":"/1k8tfoV3SKjIhJ970yhd2hKfZg=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABBE0Q2Q","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/122","origin":"github"},"title":"Field import: unh_echoboats_project11 (2026-05-01)","message":"## Field import — `unh_echoboats_project11` (2026-05-01)\n\nImports field-side commits from `gitcloud/jazzy` made during the\n2026-05-01 BizzyBoat deployment (this repo's #121). 8 commits\nmixing config tuning, launch additions, a `.gitignore` tweak, and\ntwo large per-host deployment logs (gabby and salmon).\n\n## Commits\n\n- `0674462` — `chore: ignore __pycache__/ directories`\n- `355db5d` — `docs(logs): 2026-05-01 gabby deployment log`\n- `fd1f4a4` — `feat(bizzyboat): bag local_position/* for FCU vs SBG comparison`\n- `87516d3` — `config(bizzyboat): deployment-time tuning for cameras + udp_bridge`\n- `3975a03` — `fix(bizzyboat): rename zda_launch args to avoid LaunchConfiguration collision`\n- `5aec39b` — `feat(bizzyboat): wire zda_serial_bridge into core launch`\n- `0ebc8a6` — `docs(logs): salmon 2026-05-01 — session wrap-up`\n- `96617e6` — `docs(logs): salmon 2026-05-01 — udp_bridge QoS regression debug + fix`\n\n## Substantive changes\n\n### `bizzyboat.yaml` — bridge tuning\n- Added `queue_size: 100` to all OAK camera ffmpeg / segmentation_raw\n  topic mappings on both `wifi` and `vpn` connections — addresses\n  the depth-10 ROS subscriber queue overflow seen during deployment\n  under the new MultiThreadedExecutor (rolker/udp_bridge PR #12 era).\n- Removed `oak_aft_ffmpeg` from the `vpn` connection (still on\n  `wifi`) to free uplink bandwidth against the Starlink ceiling.\n  Comment in the YAML explains the bandwidth tradeoff.\n- Added `mavros local_position/*` topics\n  (`odom`, `pose`, `velocity_local`, `velocity_body`, `accel`) to\n  the bag-recording list with a comment explaining why\n  (FCU-side counterparts to SBG's ekf_nav / ekf_quat / imu_data\n  for SBG-vs-FCU comparison at base_link, and `velocity_body` is\n  what `mru_transform` consumes to produce `/bizzy/odom`).\n\n### Launch wiring\n- New `bizzyboat_project11/launch/zda_launch.py`: composes the\n  `zda_serial_bridge` package (in `rolker/marine_tools` PR #9)\n  into the boat-side launch graph. Drives M3 serial-ZDA via gabby\n  `/dev/ttyS2`. Documented at the top.\n- `core_launch.py`: includes `zda_launch.py` in the core boat\n  launch.\n- `oak_cameras_launch.py`: `oak_forward` H.265 bitrate 1000 → 800\n  kbps for consistency with the other cameras.\n- `package.xml`: added zda dep.\n\n### `.gitignore`\n- Adds `__pycache__/` so Python build artifacts don't appear as\n  uncommitted-changes garbage in the repo (a common cause of\n  `make sync` skips today).\n\n### Launch-arg-collision fix (`3975a03`)\n- Renamed `device` / `baud` LaunchConfiguration keys in\n  `zda_launch.py` to `zda_device` / `zda_baud` to avoid a name\n  collision with `sound_speed_launch.py` (which also declares\n  `device`). Inline comment in `zda_launch.py` explains.\n\n### Deployment logs (gabby + salmon)\n- `docs/logs/2026/2026-05-01_gabby_logs.md` (1337 lines) — gabby\n  agent's full session log.\n- `docs/logs/2026/2026-05-01_salmon_logs.md` (197 lines) —\n  salmon-side log focused on the udp_bridge QoS regression\n  debugging. Per the per-host log convention.\n\n## Pre-review\n\n- **Tests**: no new code-side tests in this PR (config + launch\n  changes mostly). The new `zda_serial_bridge` package itself\n  ships tests in its own repo (rolker/marine_tools#9).\n- **Topic-name accuracy**: `local_position/*` topics added to the\n  bag-record list match what mavros publishes under `/bizzy/mavros/`\n  with the standard `local_position` plugin. Verified during\n  deployment.\n- **Idempotency**: launch-file changes follow existing patterns;\n  `core_launch.py` Include is composable.\n- **Hardcoded paths**: `/dev/ttyS2` appears as a default for\n  `zda_device` — consistent with deployment hardware. The arg\n  is overrideable.\n- **Diverged**: **No** (origin not ahead).\n\n## Cross-repo dependencies\n\nThis PR depends on:\n- [rolker/marine_tools#9](https://github.com/rolker/marine_tools/pull/9) — provides the `zda_serial_bridge` package\n- [rolker/udp_bridge#16](https://github.com/rolker/udp_bridge/pull/16) — bridge fixes that motivate the YAML `queue_size: 100` tuning\n- [rolker/camp#51](https://github.com/rolker/camp/pull/51) — operator-side QoS fix that complements the bridge default change\n\nRecommend merging in dependency order: marine_tools → udp_bridge →\ncamp → unh_echoboats_project11.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}